ACTION
Each tangent action resets valid cells to exact GP plus or minus epsilon times
the normalized radial Fourier vector, performs the real
GRAMRLevel::advance, evaluates fixture-only constraints, subtracts the
signed states, and projects the result back to the requested Fourier parity.
The production lifecycle in each signed step is framework periodic exchange,
project radial ghost fill, direct target-d=4 RHS, live gauge, fixed lapse
source, sigma=0.3 KO, outer valid-surface RHS override, locked four-stage RK,
and cleanup after each update. The signed difference cancels discrete GP
background drift.

