PROFILE AND MODE GATE
The fixture emits the normalized 18-component radial profile at all 32
cell centers for every terminal sequence. The locally aligned D12 profiles
peak at x=1.1875; smooth-bulk profiles peak at x=2.3125; inner-localized
profiles peak at the first valid cell x=0.5625. The first/last three-cell
energy fractions above demonstrate that the capped inner sequences are
boundary dominated. Nonzero per-component amplifications also differ, so the
fields do not share a common eigenvalue. Raw versus GP-field-scaled L2 rate
differences are 1.63-45.1 percent. Normalized linearized constraints are not
uniformly small.

